alembic init
- creates a file structure, edit mako script to change revision template, edit env.py to point alembic to the configured db

alembic revision --autogenerate -m"initial"
- creates a first revision, check alembic/versions
- if you have existing db before this, move it aside (or point alembic to nonexistent sqlite) to generate inital revision from the model
- re-run revision to see if your db matches the model

alembic stamp head
- stamp the current state of db as up to date without running transaction

alembic check 
- see if head is up to date

alembic current
- see current head

- after making changes to the model, create revision and then apply it to the db:
alembic upgrade head
